  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2024-02-29T01:19:31.516Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I had an entire library of custom U# scripts written in Assets/UdonSharp. After the latest SDK upgrade the SDK WIPES this ENTIRE folder and only preserved the default utility scripts. This happened on two (edit three) of my projects now. Luckily I made a backup with the second one after it happened to the first one. Should we not be storing our own scripts in Assets/UdonSharp? I haven't seen any documentation reflect this. Unsure why it would be wiping those folders outside of the Packages directory.",
